    "topic_code": "1.3",
    "topic_title": "Rates of Change and Behavior of Graphs",
    "stem": "The graph of f consists of straight line segments connecting (0, 1), (2, 7), (5, 1), and (7, 3), in that order. Which statement correctly describes the graph from x = 2 to x = 5?",
    "choices": [
     {
      "choice_key": "A",
      "choice_text": "The graph increases with an average rate of change of 2.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Sign-loss error: using only the magnitude of the slope ignores its direction. The graph falls as x increases on the requested interval, so its average rate of change is negative. Fix: Subtract endpoint outputs in the same order as endpoint inputs."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "B",
      "choice_text": "The graph decreases with an average rate of change of −6.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Output-change-only error: −6 is the change in f, not the average rate of change. The input changes by 3, so the slope is −6/3 = −2. Fix: Divide the output change by the input change."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "C",
      "choice_text": "The graph increases with an average rate of change of 2/7.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Whole-graph interval error: 2/7 is the average rate of change from x = 0 to x = 7. Those endpoints do not describe the requested interval, where the graph decreases. Fix: Identify the requested interval’s endpoints before computing its secant slope."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "D",
      "choice_text": "The graph decreases with an average rate of change of −2.",
      "is_correct": true,
      "rationale": "On this interval, the graph falls from 7 to 1 as x increases from 2 to 5. Its average rate of change is (1−7)/(5−2) = −2, matching the downward slope."
     }
    ]
   },
